  "description": "A simple glazed potato banchan you won't be able to stop making, or eating.",
  "notes": "Notes: You can use joseon ganjang (Korean soy sauce made from soy alone), yangjo ganjang (Korean soy sauce made from soy plus wheat), or even Japanese soy sauce here, if that's what you have. See our guide to the Korean pantry for more on the most common varieties of Korean soy sauce.\nLook for potatoes that are about 1 1/2 inches in diameter. If you can't find small potatoes, cut larger Yukon Golds into 1 1/2-inch pieces.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: This dish is best enjoyed immediately.",
